CLASS:: SubGrain
SUMMARY:: Subsample-accurate granular synthesis
CATEGORIES:: UGens>Generators>Granular
RELATED:: Classes/GrainBuf, Classes/TGrains, Classes/Warp1

DESCRIPTION::
SubGrain is a granular synthesis UGen with subsample-accurate grain triggering:

LIST::
## Subsample-accurate grain scheduling for smooth frequency sweeps
## Density/regularity control: morph between periodic and stochastic triggering
## Internal delay line for live input granulation
## External buffer for sample-based granulation (strong::mono buffers only::)
## Rate is sampled per-grain for precise pitch control
## Anti-aliased playback with cubic, 6-point, or sinc interpolation
## Smooth morphable envelope from percussive to hanning to reversed
## Multichannel equal-power panning with per-grain spread
::

note::
Buffer must be mono. Multi-channel buffers will be silently ignored.
Use Buffer.readChannel to load a single channel from multi-channel files.
::

SUBSECTION:: Parameter rates

All parameters except numChannels, maxGrains, and maxDelayTime can be modulated at control or audio rate. Parameters are sampled at each grain's birth.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: numChannels
Number of output channels. Must be a scalar. Default: 2.

ARGUMENT:: maxGrains
Maximum simultaneous grains (1-1024). Must be a scalar. Default: 32.

ARGUMENT:: maxDelayTime
Maximum delay time for internal delay line in seconds. Must be a scalar. Default: 1.0.

ARGUMENT:: input
Audio input signal. Written to internal delay line for live granulation.

ARGUMENT:: buffer
Buffer number for sample-based granulation. Must be mono. Use -1 for no buffer.

ARGUMENT:: bufferMix
Mix between delay line and buffer. 0 = delay only, 1 = buffer only. Default: 1.0.

ARGUMENT:: density
Grain trigger rate in grains per second. 0 = no new grains (silence). Default: 10.

ARGUMENT:: regularity
Trigger regularity. 1 = perfectly periodic, 0 = stochastic (Dust-like). Default: 1.0.

ARGUMENT:: duration
Grain duration in seconds. Default: 0.1.

ARGUMENT:: rate
Playback rate, sampled per grain. Default: 1.0.

ARGUMENT:: position
Position in buffer/delay [0-1]. For buffer: 0 = start, 1 = end. For delay line: 0 = oldest (max delay), 1 = newest (min delay). Use values close to 1.0 for responsive live granulation. Default: 0.5.

ARGUMENT:: positionSpread
Random deviation from position per grain. Default: 0.

ARGUMENT:: envShape
Envelope shape [0-1]. Smoothly morphs between: 0 = sharp attack with long exponential decay (percussive), 0.5 = symmetric hanning window, 1 = long exponential attack with sharp decay (reversed percussive). Default: 0.5.

ARGUMENT:: pan
Pan position [0-1]. For stereo: 0 = left, 1 = right. Default: 0.5.

ARGUMENT:: panSpread
Random deviation from pan position per grain. Default: 0.

ARGUMENT:: interpolation
Interpolation mode. 0 = cubic (4-point, efficient), 1 = 6-point polynomial (good balance), 2 = sinc (8-tap windowed with anti-aliasing for pitch-up). Default: 0.

RETURNS::
An array of numChannels audio signals.


EXAMPLES::

SUBSECTION:: Buffer granulation

code::
// Load a mono buffer
b = Buffer.readChannel(s, Platform.resourceDir +/+ "sounds/a11wlk01.wav", channels: [0]);

// Simple granular cloud
(
{
    SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        buffer: b,
        bufferMix: 1,
        density: 20,
        duration: 0.08,
        rate: 1,
        position: MouseX.kr(0, 1),
        positionSpread: 0.05,
        envShape: 0.5,  // hanning
        panSpread: 0.3
    ) * 0.5
}.play;
)

// Pitch shifting granular
(
{
    SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        buffer: b,
        bufferMix: 1,
        density: 50,
        duration: 0.05,
        rate: MouseY.kr(0.5, 2),  // pitch control
        position: LFSaw.kr(0.1).range(0, 1),
        envShape: 0.5,
        interpolation: 2  // sinc for clean pitch shifting
    ) * 0.4
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Live input granulation

note::
For the delay line: position 1 = newest audio (min delay), position 0 = oldest (max delay).
Use position close to 1.0 for responsive live granulation.
The delay buffer needs time to fill - with position 0.5 and maxDelayTime 2.0, you need to wait ~1 second before hearing output.
::

code::
// Granulate microphone input (responsive - short delay)
(
{
    var input = SoundIn.ar(0);
    SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        maxDelayTime: 1.0,
        input: input,
        buffer: -1,       // no buffer
        bufferMix: 0,     // delay line only
        density: 15,
        duration: 0.15,
        rate: 1,
        position: 0.95,   // newest audio (~50ms delay)
        positionSpread: 0.05,
        envShape: 0.3,    // slightly percussive
        panSpread: 0.4
    ) * 0.6
}.play;
)

// Live granulation with longer delay (wait ~1s for buffer to fill)
(
{
    var input = SoundIn.ar(0);
    SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        maxDelayTime: 2.0,
        input: input,
        buffer: -1,
        bufferMix: 0,
        density: 12,
        duration: 0.2,
        rate: 1,
        position: 0.5,    // ~1 second delay
        positionSpread: 0.2,
        envShape: 0.5,
        panSpread: 0.5
    ) * 0.5
}.play;
)

// Live input with pitch randomization
(
{
    var input = SoundIn.ar(0);
    SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        maxDelayTime: 1.0,
        input: input,
        bufferMix: 0,
        density: 25,
        duration: 0.1,
        rate: TExpRand.kr(0.8, 1.25, Impulse.kr(25)),  // random pitch per grain
        position: LFNoise1.kr(0.5).range(0.85, 0.98),  // near-newest audio
        positionSpread: 0.05,
        envShape: 0.5,
        panSpread: 0.6
    ) * 0.5
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Hybrid: buffer + live crossfade

code::
b = Buffer.readChannel(s, Platform.resourceDir +/+ "sounds/a11wlk01.wav", channels: [0]);

// Crossfade between buffer and live input
(
{
    var input = SoundIn.ar(0);
    var mix = MouseX.kr(0, 1);  // 0 = live, 1 = buffer
    
    SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        maxDelayTime: 1.0,
        input: input,
        buffer: b,
        bufferMix: mix,
        density: 20,
        duration: 0.1,
        rate: 1,
        position: 0.9,    // for live: near-newest; for buffer: near-end
        positionSpread: 0.1,
        envShape: 0.5,
        panSpread: 0.3
    ) * 0.5
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Regularity morphing

code::
b = Buffer.readChannel(s, Platform.resourceDir +/+ "sounds/a11wlk01.wav", channels: [0]);

// Morph from periodic to stochastic with MouseX
(
{
    SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        buffer: b,
        density: 50,
        regularity: MouseX.kr(0, 1),  // left = chaotic, right = periodic
        duration: 0.02,
        rate: 1,
        position: 0.5,
        positionSpread: 0.3,
        envShape: 0.2,  // percussive
        panSpread: 0.5
    ) * 0.5
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Envelope shapes

code::
b = Buffer.readChannel(s, Platform.resourceDir +/+ "sounds/a11wlk01.wav", channels: [0]);

// Morph envelope from percussive to hanning to reversed
(
{
    SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        buffer: b,
        density: 8,
        duration: 0.3,
        rate: 1,
        position: 0.3,
        positionSpread: 0.1,
        envShape: MouseX.kr(0, 1),  // 0=percussive, 0.5=hanning, 1=reversed
        panSpread: 0.4
    ) * 0.4
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Subsample frequency smoothness

code::
b = Buffer.readChannel(s, Platform.resourceDir +/+ "sounds/a11wlk01.wav", channels: [0]);

// Smooth frequency sweep - no stepping artifacts
(
{
    var freq = XLine.kr(10, 200, 10);
    SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        buffer: b,
        density: freq,
        duration: 0.05,
        rate: 1,
        position: 0.5,
        positionSpread: 0.02,
        envShape: 0.5,
        panSpread: 0.2
    ) * 0.4
}.play;
)

// Audio-rate density modulation for FM-like effects
(
{
    var densityMod = SinOsc.ar(5).range(20, 200);
    SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        buffer: b,
        density: densityMod,
        duration: 0.02,
        rate: 1,
        position: 0.3,
        envShape: 0.5,
        panSpread: 0.3
    ) * 0.3
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Interpolation comparison

code::
b = Buffer.readChannel(s, Platform.resourceDir +/+ "sounds/a11wlk01.wav", channels: [0]);

// Compare interpolation modes (use headphones)
// 0 = cubic (fastest), 1 = 6-point, 2 = sinc (best for pitch shifting)
(
{
    var rate = MouseY.kr(0.25, 4, 1);  // pitch shift
    var interp = MouseX.kr(0, 2).round;  // interpolation mode
    
    SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        buffer: b,
        density: 30,
        duration: 0.08,
        rate: rate,
        position: 0.5,
        positionSpread: 0.1,
        envShape: 0.5,
        interpolation: interp
    ) * 0.4
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Multichannel output

code::
b = Buffer.readChannel(s, Platform.resourceDir +/+ "sounds/a11wlk01.wav", channels: [0]);

// 8-channel granular spatialization
(
{
    var sig = SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 8,
        maxGrains: 64,
        buffer: b,
        density: 30,
        duration: 0.15,
        rate: LFNoise1.kr(0.3).range(0.9, 1.1),
        position: LFNoise1.kr(0.2).range(0, 1),
        positionSpread: 0.1,
        envShape: 0.5,
        pan: LFSaw.kr(0.1).range(0, 1),  // rotating pan
        panSpread: 0.2
    );
    // Mix down to stereo for monitoring
    Splay.ar(sig) * 0.4
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Feedback granulation

code::
// Granular feedback loop (wait a moment for delay to fill)
(
{
    var in = LocalIn.ar(2);
    var sig = SubGrain.ar(
        numChannels: 2,
        maxDelayTime: 1.0,
        input: in.sum,
        buffer: -1,
        bufferMix: 0,
        density: 8,
        regularity: 0.9,
        duration: 0.3,
        rate: 0.99,
        position: 0.7,    // ~0.3 second delay
        positionSpread: 0.15,
        envShape: 0.2,
        panSpread: 0.3
    );
    LocalOut.ar(
        (Impulse.ar(0) * 0.5) + (sig * 0.7)
    );
    sig * 0.5
}.play;
)
::

